<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.get(i)));</code>

However, the above assertion checks element-wise equality assuming both the list and the collection maintain the same order, which is correct in this context since `addAll` preserves the order. But we need to ensure the size of the list matches the size of the collection and also handle the case when the collection is empty. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert this.size() == c.size() && (\forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i &amp;&amp; i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i &amp;&amp; i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
